{{C|Omniscience}} is a 4 (3 if upgraded) {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It allows you to select one card in your draw pile, which it will play twice and {{KW|Exhaust}}, without expending any {{Icon|RE}}. Both copies of an X-cost card played this way will use the {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' you have after playing {{C|Omniscience}} for X, without consuming that {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy'''. {{C|Omniscience}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.

== Interactions ==
=== Synergies ===
* Using {{C|Omniscience}} to play another copy of {{C|Omniscience}} that is in your draw pile will result in 2 cards being played and doubled. {{C|Omniscience}} can be chained in this way to theorethically play your entire draw pile.
* {{C|Omniscience}} increases the counter of {{BD|Time Warp}} as normal, but bypasses its forced end of turn. This means that if an {{C|Omniscience}} is played as the 12th card, its full effects, including a possible {{C|Omniscience}} chain, will take effect before your turn is ended.
** However, playing an {{C|Omniscience}} as the 11th card and targeting a card that is not {{C|Omniscience}} will result in only one copy of that card being played.

=== Neutral ===
* Since {{C|Indignation}} and {{C|Inner Peace}} both have different effects depending on your current {{KW|Stance}}, and both of them can put you into their respective {{KW|Stance}}, targeting either of these cards with {{C|Omniscience}} can result in two different effects happening.
* Unlike {{BD|Time Warp}}, which forces an end of turn, {{C|Normality}} and {{R|Velvet Choker}} enforce a limit on the amount of cards played, which {{C|Omniscience}} cannot bypass. 
* {{R|Strange Spoon}} has a 50% chance of saving a card that would be {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} by {{C|Omniscience}}.

=== Anti-Synergies ===
* Targeting a card that ends your turn, such as {{C|Meditate}} or {{C|Vault}}, will end your turn after the first copy played and not play a second copy or any remaining cards of an {{C|Omniscience}} chain.
* Targeting a card that requires certain conditions to be met for that card to have an effect, such as {{C|Signature Move}}, without meeting those requirements will result in the card being played and {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}}, but not in the effects of that card taking place.

