{{C|Ritual Dagger}} is a 1 {{Icon|CE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Special|Special}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 15 damage, and if this damage is {{KW|Fatal}}, it will permanently increase this damage by 3 (5 if upgraded). {{C|Ritual Dagger}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.

== Obtaining Ritual Dagger ==
* {{C|Ritual Dagger}} is an Event Card, and the only way to obtain one is through the event {{E|The Nest}}.

* {{R|Dolly's Mirror}} can duplicate your Ritual Dagger, giving you a second copy. Do note that activating a Ritual Dagger will ''not'' affect any other copies you may have in your deck. However, the damage on the card ''will'' be copied over at the time of initial duplication, so if done late in the run, it will give a second huge Attack.

== Interactions ==
=== Synergies ===
* As playing {{C|Ritual Dagger}} at the right moment is crucial, it synergizes with {{R|Runic Pyramid}} and ways to {{KW|Retain}} it, such as {{C|Well-Laid Plans}}, {{C|Equilibrium}} or {{C|Meditate}}.

* As one of the few cards that has benefits that remain outside of combat, triggering it as often as possible becomes an additional objective within combat. Given that {{C|Ritual Dagger}} {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} after use, it synergizes with:
** {{R|Strange Spoon}}, which gives a 50% chance to not {{KW|Exhaust}} {{C|Ritual Dagger}} when played, allowing it to be redrawn and used again.
** {{C|Exhume}}, which can get {{C|Ritual Dagger}} back once after being played, with the added benefit of putting it directly into your hand.

=== Neutral ===
* If a {{C|Ritual Dagger}} is stored using the {{E|A Note For Yourself}} event, it will not keep the damage increases, and will always do 15 damage when retrieved. As with all cards, it will retain its {{KW|Upgrade}} status.

* When duplicated through an effect such as {{C|Double Tap}} or a {{P|Duplication Potion}}, {{C|Ritual Dagger}} will trigger its {{KW|Fatal}} effect even if only the second play was {{KW|Fatal}}.
** As duplicated {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} always target the same enemy with both plays, you cannot trigger {{C|Ritual Dagger}} twice by duplicating it.

* {{KW|Fatal}} does ''not'' trigger when {{BD|Minion|Minions}} are killed.
** However, the {{M|Cultist}} enemies in {{M|Awakened One}} fight are not technically {{BD|Minion|Minions}}, and ''can'' trigger {{KW|Fatal}}.

* {{KW|Fatal}} is not affected by {{M|Slime Boss}} or other Slime enemies splitting, and only triggers when reducing a Slime's health to 0, whether that Slime was spawned as the result of a split or not.
* The first phase of {{M|Awakened One}} does not trigger {{KW|Fatal}}, but the second phase does.

* In the {{M|Darkling|Three Darklings}} fight, an attack is only considered {{KW|Fatal}} if it kills the last {{M|Darkling}}; otherwise, unlimited triggers could be farmed on this fight.

* {{KW|Fatal}} triggers on killing the {{M|Corrupt Heart}}, although this does not matter, as it ends the run.

=== Anti-Synergies ===
* Due to the limited number of {{KW|Fatal}} triggers available in any given combat, {{C|Ritual Dagger}} does not synergize with other {{KW|Fatal}} cards:
==== Cards ====
* {{C|Hand of Greed}}
* {{C|Feed}}
* {{C|Lesson Learned}}

== Trivia ==
* A {{C|Ritual Dagger}} can be seen stuck in the {{M|Awakened One}}'s chest.

